after some uncertainty the Obamacare  repeal in the US Senate is dead again  Republicans totally unable to unite  behind a plan to get rid of the  Affordable Care Act after threatening to  do it promising to do it for most of  Barack Obama's presidency we saw  Republican susan collins republican  republican lisa murkowski and of course  republican senator john mccain vote  against the repeal Trump saying that the  three had let the American people down  the last iteration that they tried was  what's being called a skinny repeal the  skinny repeal would have led not to the  reduction in obesity rates as the word  skinny might suggest but rather it would  have led to 16 million people losing  health insurance by 2026 as well as an  increase in premiums of 20% above and  beyond the current projections Senator  John McCain recently diagnosed with  brain cancer has been getting a ton of  attention around his vote against this  and Mike Pence was seen talking to  McCain for about 20 minutes right before  the vote but then McCain went over to a  group of Democrats who all seemed  thrilled to see him walk over and  ultimately McCain voting against this  repeal now I get that McCain's vote was  somewhat of a surprise but I think  people are going a little overboard Pat  and calling McCain the hero here I mean  Collins and Murkowski are just as  responsible for this as McCain all of  the other Democrats on to which these  three Republican votes were added to are  just as responsible for this as is John  McCain and by the way what about the  people that created Obamacare including  the former President Barack Obama yeah  John McCain has somewhat of a conscience  and that does distinguish him from a lot  of the Republican Party right now but it  doesn't making the savior here well sure  but I think we knew that all 48  Democrats would vote against any  Obamacare repeal efforts and as far as  Republicans are concerned I mean Susan  Collins and Lisa Murkowski were pretty  certain knows as well we just didn't  know which moderate was going to join  them if any if it was going to be McCain  or taffeta or Heller but that might have  someone that's my point which is while  it was surprising and sort of unknown  until the last moment  it's not anymore heroic and what I'm  thinking about more and more is Joe  Biden reportedly lobbied John McCain  before this vote which is interesting  and I believe it's time for John McCain  to leave the Republican Party not  because he's some progressive panacea  but because he's just not radical enough  to be in the Republican Party there's  lots of center-right in the Democratic  Party right now and John McCain once  considered leaving the Republican Party  I don't think there's really much of a  place for McCain in the Republican Party  right now well it seems like a lot of  Republicans voted for this knowing that  it would never actually be signed into  law because the next step would be to  join it with the House bill in  conference but I think McCain was  concerned because the house could just  pass the skinny bill as well and then  that goes to the president's desk and he  didn't want that to happen so in that  regard I think he did stand on principle  here  well that principle to whatever extent  it was heroic as it's being portrayed by  some did lead to the situation we have  now and the next question is what next  right  Obama care seems sort of like it's not  just this thing but it's part of our  health care system now it's not some  crazy appendage it's been around for  seven years it's by and large a you know  furthering the same for-profit insurance  system that we have but it did some good  things Trump and the Republican  establishment are really the losers here  and now they will do everything they can  to make Obamacare fail we might have  news about that in the next day or two  Obamacare is not in a death spiral it's  having the exact same issues that all of  health insurance is which is rising  premiums people who still can't afford  care there's nothing particularly  disastrous about Obama care it sucks  like our entire health care system sucks  just in slightly mitigated ways by  increasing the risk pool and increasing  some subsidies so what's next for Trump  Obamacare repeal is dead the travel ban  is in limbo at best tax reform is on the  back burner for now although some  Republicans are saying that's what they  want to get back into next the wall with  Mexico is laughable and Trump's new  NAFTA deal is really similar to the TPP  proposal that Donald Trump was against I  genuinely don't know what's next here  which is why and we're going to talk  about North Korea more in the next  segment which is why I am worried that  six months into his presidency Trump is  a pseudo lame duck and what now could  happen is an erratic or desperate move  to get himself involved in a military  escalation the top candidate right now  would be North Korea Syria is a  possibility Iran is a possibility and  that's why I'm really scared about the  next six months for Trump that is  interesting especially because it feels  as if Democrats are trying to run out  the clock and succeeding and doing so  already a quarter of the way to the  midterms and you think about what issues  he might be able to win on not many  because a lot of these bills you can't  just hide in Budget Reconciliation you  need 60 votes for say tax reform correct  I think the move here is maybe to go for  infrastructure because you can get  Democrats on board with that as well  maybe and Trump does want to do it in a  totally sort of capital crony capitalist  equate with handouts to all those  construction and real estate buddies but  if Democrats can get some compromise on  some issues that they want pet projects  whatever then that could be a  possibility Trump is going to need to  rebuild his influence and credibility  now particularly if Jeff session goes  and one of trumps last links to the  mainline Republican Party is sessions  right now so what happens if in one  session goes and this is why I'm worried  that this could push Trump into  haphazard and very erratic action with  maybe the top candidate North Korea if  not Syria or Iran and we'll talk about  that a little bit later in the program  I'm on Twitter at D Pakman follow me  there send me your thoughts there we'll  be back after the break  today's program is made possible in part  by blue apron the number-one fresh  ingredient and recipe delivery service  in the country for under 10 bucks a meal  they deliver seasonal recipes with  pre-portioned ingredients right to your  door I've been cooking with blue apron  now for over a year and I love it and I  love not wasting food I don't have to  figure out what to do with that extra  package of cilantro they send me the  exact amount of cilantro that the recipe  calls for no waste  at all it's also completely flexible so  you can customize your recipes it's each  week depending on your diet you can  choose delivery options that fit your  needs and they have the blue apron  freshness guarantee which promises every  ingredient arrives ready to cook or they  will make it right for you some of the  meals available in the coming month  include basil pesto chicken with summer  vegetable panzanella sauteed shrimp and  green beans with globe tomatoes spinach  and orzo pasta whole grain pasta and  summer vegetables with heirloom tomato  caprese salad and miso butter salmon and  lo mein noodles with cucumber and charm  tomatoes you can check out this week's  menu get your first three meals free  with free shipping by going to blue  apron comm slash Pakman support our  sponsors and support the David Pakman  show  three meals free with free shipping at  blue apron dot-com /pa k ma n
 

